content:
{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "type": "feature",
  "problem": [
    {
      "text": "The README motivates ExLlamaV3 as a rewrite: treating newer architectures as Llama variants had become restrictive, while V2's process design and EXL2 input-channel permutation complicated parallel inference.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_d87dfb96e20f427387774b20461e5303"]
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": [
    {
      "text": "This change introduces an early-preview inference framework spanning architecture-specific models, EXL3 conversion and execution, queued generation, and installation/evaluation tooling. See the linked chapters for each subsystem.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_d87dfb96e20f427387774b20461e5303", "call_91f94bda0f9843a694ae6921629c67c4", "call_4fb744a7442543378c02bda9ce8f1a24", "call_a97f254e6c0a4ba2ac5b86c45ccf5beb"]
    }
  ],
  "impact": [
    {
      "text": "Users gain a documented model-conversion workflow and inference examples, but this preview explicitly lacks tensor parallelism, cache quantization, multimodal support and ROCm support; FlashAttention-2 is required.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_d87dfb96e20f427387774b20461e5303"]
    }
  ],
  "source_notes": [
    {
      "text": "The documentation describes EXL3 as a QTIP variant using a procedural codebook and tail-biting trellises, with different regularization and packing. Performance and accuracy statements there are published claims, not measurements reproduced here.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_8f846bec1df74e668f9ee78b483be3df"]
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No builds, tests, conversions or benchmarks were run.",
    "Coverage is selective: native kernel internals, quantizer mathematics, tokenizer and loader implementation, cache/page-table internals, individual architecture implementations, and evaluation/test scripts were not fully inspected.",
    "Binary benchmark figures and bundled calibration/Hadamard data were not inspected; no quantitative performance or accuracy conclusion is independently established."
  ],
  "links": ["c0de1b3c5a7f9d2e4a6b8c0d2e4f6a8b1c3d5e7f", "c0de2a4c6e8f0b1d3a5c7e9f1b3d5a7c9e1f3b5d", "c0de3f5a7b9c1d2e4f6a8b0c2d4e6f8a1b3c5d7e", "c0de4b6d8f0a2c3e5b7d9f1a3c5e7b9d1f3a5c7e"],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "c0de1b3c5a7f9d2e4a6b8c0d2e4f6a8b1c3d5e7f",
      "title": "Model architecture and execution",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "The architecture registry maps Llama, Mistral, Qwen2, Phi3 and Gemma2 causal-LM identifiers to separate configuration and model classes.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_91f94bda0f9843a694ae6921629c67c4"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The common Model executes an ordered module list, preparing inputs for each module's device. Prefill stops at the last KV-producing module rather than executing the complete logits path.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_d785deacc62a4fe69b0ff3e4f1a60e92"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c0de2a4c6e8f0b1d3a5c7e9f1b3d5a7c9e1f3b5d",
      "title": "EXL3 conversion and quantized execution",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "Conversion proceeds module by module on CUDA: capture calibration statistics, allocate bitrates, convert linear layers, save tensors, advance calibration states, and unload the module. Checkpoints retain the next module index, bit surplus and activation state; resumption is explicit.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_4fb744a7442543378c02bda9ce8f1a24"]
        },
        {
          "text": "LinearEXL3 applies a Hadamard input transform and selects either reconstructed weights with half-precision GEMM or the native EXL3 GEMM path. Reconstruction defaults to inputs with at least 32 flattened rows and can be overridden through parameters.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_02c763524131406983a23460bfdb4b6e"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c0de3f5a7b9c1d2e4f6a8b0c2d4e6f8a1b3c5d7e",
      "title": "Queued generation",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "Generator connects model, cache, tokenizer and page table with pending/active job queues, batching and prefill chunk controls. Its interface supports cancellation and optional draft-model speculative decoding, requiring equal main and draft cache capacities.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_a97f254e6c0a4ba2ac5b86c45ccf5beb"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c0de4b6d8f0a2c3e5b7d9f1a3c5e7b9d1f3a5c7e",
      "title": "Packaging and evaluation documentation",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "setup.py gathers native C/C++/CUDA sources into a PyTorch CUDAExtension, with EXLLAMA_NOCOMPILE disabling installation-time compilation. The README documents this as the JIT installation option.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_abfc72a69ce04063b2dbc31688b54a35", "call_d87dfb96e20f427387774b20461e5303"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The EXL3 document links perplexity comparisons and HumanEval tooling, distinguishing bitrate plots from weight-memory plots and excluding embedding memory from the latter.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_8f846bec1df74e668f9ee78b483be3df"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
